1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,798
"Breakfast is the most important meal of the day."

2
00:00:02,798 --> 00:00:04,397
Guess who said it first?

3
00:00:04,397 --> 00:00:05,790
Not a doctor.

4
00:00:05,790 --> 00:00:08,547
A health magazine, printed in 1917...

5
00:00:08,547 --> 00:00:09,801
...at the resort of the

6
00:00:09,801 --> 00:00:12,193
man who co-invented corn flakes.

7
00:00:12,193 --> 00:00:14,016
Then, in the 1920s,

8
00:00:14,016 --> 00:00:15,780
a meatpacker hired a PR man

9
00:00:15,780 --> 00:00:16,910
to sell more bacon.

10
00:00:16,910 --> 00:00:18,071
He didn't buy ads.

11
00:00:18,071 --> 00:00:19,174
He asked one doctor:

12
00:00:19,174 --> 00:00:20,915
light breakfast, or heavy?

13
00:00:20,915 --> 00:00:21,793
"Heavy."

14
00:00:21,793 --> 00:00:22,443
Then that doctor

15
00:00:22,443 --> 00:00:24,351
wrote to 5,000 physicians.

16
00:00:24,351 --> 00:00:26,917
About 4,500 agreed.

17
00:00:26,917 --> 00:00:29,011
At least, that's how he told it.

18
00:00:29,011 --> 00:00:30,485
Newspapers ran it.

19
00:00:30,485 --> 00:00:32,436
And the heartiest breakfast?

20
00:00:32,436 --> 00:00:33,908
Bacon and eggs.

21
00:00:33,908 --> 00:00:35,673
The doctors never picked the menu.

22
00:00:35,673 --> 00:00:37,797
The bacon seller did.

23
00:00:37,797 --> 00:00:40,053
And, he said, his sales went up.

24
00:00:40,053 --> 00:00:41,539
Eat it or skip it.

25
00:00:41,539 --> 00:00:42,970
Just know who wrote the slogan.
